			"25": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "choice",
						"value": "Left"
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "number",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "text",
						"value": "ROTATION\n\nThe Rotation node outputs the rotation of each incoming slice as a period (float).\n\nIn this patch we take an arbitrary amount of slices, we want their rotation which we convert from period to  degrees using the Angle Converter. We take the angle and the indices of the slices and concatenate them into a good looking string before merging it into a single string with a breakpoint as seperator(click on the Merge node and check the node panel). The string gets rendered and send out. In Arena this source gives you  on-screen info of the rotation of each slice which could be useful when videomapping."
					}
				},
